{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/339881-demon-in-a-goblin-market","id":339881,"title":"Demon in a goblin market","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-14T02:35:11-08:00","id":339881,"title":"Demon in a goblin market","content":"A bit of a question that though it fits into changeling fits into the demon forums better is how would a goblin market effect a demon? From the various effects let us first go how one can literally trade for memories in a goblin market. The extraction to sell or drinking to receive.<br /> now question one: would a demon selling a cover's memories erode the cover?<br /> 1b:could a demon sell memories that it did not itself physically experience or would memories of the cover be sell-able?<br /> <br /> Question two:Could a demon accept second hand skills<br /> 2b:could a hobgoblin or other market merchant accept a demon's contract?<br /> <br /> Question three: would goblin fruit effect a demon in cover like a human?<br /> <br /> Mostly all I can think of being of any real impact in a crossover game, any input would be appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T02:46:20-08:00","id":339902,"title":"","content":"Another good question would be if being in the Hedge or in Arcadia could lessen the compromise penalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T02:52:07-08:00","id":339906,"title":"","content":"well considering you can't use rip the gates to leave could the agents of the machine only make a one way trip too if you gained the hunted condition if you experienced compromise bad enough if compromise was not lessened?<br /> <br /> rabbit hole that me n my st fell into was &quot;what effect would the thorns have?&quot; so maybe it is safer to just stay out of the hedge lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T07:43:31-08:00","id":339993,"title":"","content":"My intuition is that selling a cover's memories only erodes that cover if it would be particularly strange for the cover to do so, since selling memories at a Goblin Market is something a human can do normally. I'd also say that a demon can sell cover-memories rather than lived ones, since the cover is jacked-in to reality enough that the memories are basically real anyway. However, a goblin merchant might find something sketchy about them (especially if your Cover rating is low), accusing you of trying to offload some knockoff memories or something similar. Honestly, if you're doing a scene where a demon is selling memories, I'd focus more on the psychological effects of how a being with perfect recall feels about suddenly having holes in their mind.<br /> <br /> Goblins would eat pacts up, I think. I mean, they probably couldn't access the Primum of the artifact (since it's connected to reality in a way fae things aren't), but a written, transferable agreement for a human's soul? <i>Gimme.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T16:57:41-08:00","id":341373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/339881-demon-in-a-goblin-market?p=339906#post339906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well considering you can't use rip the gates to leave could the agents of the machine only make a one way trip too if you gained the hunted condition if you experienced compromise bad enough if compromise was not lessened?<br /> <br /> rabbit hole that me n my st fell into was &quot;what effect would the thorns have?&quot; so maybe it is safer to just stay out of the hedge lol</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they would just shred the Demon's Cover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T17:06:43-08:00","id":341377,"title":"","content":"What I want to know is what would happen if one of the Unchained made a very interesting- and tempting -Pact. A Demon can Pact virtually anything- memories, relationships, events in the life. So, the obvious niche- to my mind -of a Demon in the Goblin Market would be to buy Durances. Think about it- the Changeling hands over one or two good or not so good things about their mortal life, and the Demon undoes the worst thing that's ever happened to them. Of course, I foresee two problems with this. One- the Demon would quite possibly go insane; unlike mortals, they can't conveniently forget traumatic events and only have them come back in flashes of nightmares and all the other baggage of a Changeling. Two- the massive metaphysical and causal shift that follows would almost certainly be a massive compromise to a Demon's Cover. Can't get more noticeable than undoing a huge stretch of time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T17:15:12-08:00","id":341387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/339881-demon-in-a-goblin-market?p=341377#post341377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I want to know is what would happen if one of the Unchained made a very interesting- and tempting -Pact. A Demon can Pact virtually anything- memories, relationships, events in the life. So, the obvious niche- to my mind -of a Demon in the Goblin Market would be to buy Durances. Think about it- the Changeling hands over one or two good or not so good things about their mortal life, and the Demon undoes the worst thing that's ever happened to them. Of course, I foresee two problems with this. One- the Demon would quite possibly go insane; unlike mortals, they can't conveniently forget traumatic events and only have them come back in flashes of nightmares and all the other baggage of a Changeling. Two- the massive metaphysical and causal shift that follows would almost certainly be a massive compromise to a Demon's Cover. Can't get more noticeable than undoing a huge stretch of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>The trouble with this is that it's in direct contradiction with what happens when a demon calls in a soul pact for a supernatural being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T17:28:36-08:00","id":341396,"title":"","content":"Really? Huh. It's been a while since I've read that section- I've probably forgotten if they addressed that idea or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T18:32:53-08:00","id":341422,"title":"","content":"When a demon calls in the soul pact of a supernatural being, they gain a mortal cover, and take damage based on how big the supernaturals power trait.<br /> <br /> To my mind, it calls into question how effective such a cover is. I mean I feel sharing a cover with a fetch, or an identity that should have died during the bubonic plague don't really sound like higher level covers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T15:29:08-08:00","id":348590,"title":"","content":"Demons and Goblin Markets seem like they would go together like peanut butter and jelly, because both can trade in ephemeral things. This allows the demon more options than the average consumer, because they can sell anything they have contracted for, even things not woven into any cover yet. And can stock up on things before coming to the market.<br /> <br /> They can buy elements to add to a cover. They can even make spare entire Covers to sell on the market to sell at a markup, and offer bespoke Cover services there.<br /> <br /> They can sell their glitches instead of needing to find repair infrastructure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3698-bramble_thorn","name":"Bramble_Thorn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}